ifficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further education.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nWe need to consider criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nLet's weigh.\n\nReliability: C is known 100% reliable. A unknown. B conscientious (reliability). D takes responsibility seriously (maybe reliability). So C strong.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well. D responds to unexpected events adequately (maybe). A anticipates dangerous situations (maybe). C quick decisions (maybe). B strongest.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. B excellent computer skills, weather assessment. D solves problems extremely well, concentration. Could be any.\n\nDecision quality: C makes correct decisions quickly. A anticipates dangerous situations. D solves problems extremely well. B maybe.\n\nCrew cooperation: C creates positive atmosphere. B uncooperative. D arrogant. A leadership but maybe not. So C strongest.\n\nCommunication: C difficulty communicating ideas (weak). B can be grumpy (maybe communication). D arrogant (communication). A not mentioned. So all have issues.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously. A leadership. B conscientious. C reliable.\n\nAdaptability/feedback: A not good at taking criticism (weak). B can be grumpy (maybe). C not willing to further education (weak). D arrogant (weak). So all have concerns.\n\nOverall, C has reliability and crew cooperation, decision quality, but communication and adaptability issues. B has stress resilience, conscientiousness, but uncooperative and grumpy. D has problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership. A has anticipation, spatial vision, leadership, but unorganized and poor at criticism.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? For long-distance pilot, crew cooperation and reliability are crucial. C's reliability and positive crew atmosphere are strong. Communication difficulty is concerning, but maybe can be mitigated. However, his egocentric and unwillingness to further education could be risk. B's stress handling is important for long flights, but uncooperative is serious. D's problem solving and responsibility are good, but arrogance and weak leadership could affect crew.\n\nProbably C is strongest overall due to reliability and crew cooperation, despite communication issues. Let's propose recommendation for Candidate C, but note concerns.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion (none) but can say \"Given we have not yet discussed, I propose...\". Provide evidence.\n\nProceed."}
